Docker CLI (Command Line Interface) is the command-line tool used to communicate with Docker.

For example:

docker ps - Shows currently running containers.

docker --version - Check Docker Version

docker info - detailed information about docker

docker help - for Docker commands list

docker pull - from registry to local machine image download 

docker images - see downloaded images 

docker run -d nginx - Detached mode. The container runs in the background.

docker ps -a - show all  containers

docker stop name - Stop the container.

docker start web - stopped containers again start 

docker restart web - Useful when you want to restart an existing container.

docker rm web - remove the container

docker rm -f web - You can force-remove a running container

docker rmi nginx / docker image rm nginx - remove the image

docker logs container-name - for see logs 

docker logs -f resolvehub-backend - New logs keep appearing

docker exec -it my-container sh - You want to execute a command inside the container.

docker inspect my-container - Need detailed metadata about a container? This returns detailed JSON.

docker stats - You can see live metrics

docker cp - Copy files between host and container.

Host → Container:
docker cp ./file.txt my-container:/app/file.txt
Container → Host:
docker cp my-container:/app/log.txt ./log.txt

docker system prune - Cleanup command

docker system prune -a - is more aggressive.

docker create nginx - This creates a container but does not start it.

docker build -t resolvehub-backend:1.0 .

docker run --name backend-new resolvehub-backend:1.0

for creating volume 

docker volume create mysql-data - after

docker run -d \
  --name mysql \
  -v mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql \
  mysql